[h1]Phobos Spacer Stories[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.3.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - held draft, awaiting owner review in the game

Ships need fuel, crews need supper, and a good contract still has to leave time to come home. Phobos Spacer Stories expands life around vanilla Ostranauts with station neighbours, freight work, families, salvage histories and corporate pressure, alongside the people and companies behind Phobos equipment.

[h2]What it adds[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Company histories[/b] for the makers behind Phobos equipment: Rivetline, Ablatine, Asterel, Verdemorrow Agronomics, Fennmark, Tolvane, Lixivar, Oxsmith, Alembrine, Slingwright and Halewright. Read them in the game's encyclopedia under Makers and brands and Life between stations.
[*][b]Vanilla world stories[/b] about K-Leg freight, Ceres housing, unfinished lunar work, maintenance visas, Deimos night shifts, Venusian losses, family letters around the Atlantis blockade and the people around Titan launches.
[*][b]TV news and adverts[/b] among the game's own. Local stories receive more weight, and completed correspondence has outcome news that waits until it happens.
[*][b]Crew talk[/b]: jokes, complaints, worries and old stories in the game's own chatter. Your crew talk about your ship; people on a station talk about their own.
[*][b]Loading lore[/b] on the game's loading screens.
[*][b]22 correspondence chains[/b] in the GOALS list, with home stations, named correspondents and 23 readable archive files on data cards. Three new comparisons have shorter paths for relevant skills.
[*][b]Work that allows for the journey[/b]. New local correspondence has no expiry. Reading a freight comparison opens an optional letter to Titan's shipyards that waits for your own route, with no return deadline. Its 600-credit receipt is an extra along the way, not payment for a dedicated voyage.
[/list]
News introduces the new chains before they can start at their home stations. Most new stories need only Framework; equipment stories appear with the relevant Phobos mods. Chains take no money or goods. Two new once-only fees total 900 credits, and the archives arrive on data cards. Vanilla Gig Nexus jobs, rewards and deadlines are unchanged.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5 and Phobos Framework 0.114.0 or newer, with its BepInEx Mod Loader setup.
[*]Optional: any other Phobos mods, for the stories about their equipment.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Spacer Stories and Phobos Framework, with the BepInEx Mod Loader Framework needs.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load.
[*]Check that both are enabled in the MODS screen.
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ordinary saves are supported. It adds no items, machines or plugin: only story files that Phobos Framework reads.
[*]Removing it is safe: its talk, news, tips and articles stop appearing, unfinished goals finish and disappear on the next load, and any of its data files left on a card read as corrupted.
[*]Dismissing one of its goals in the GOALS list sets that chain aside in that save.
[*]The people, companies and incidents are original Phobos fiction alongside the game's lore, not official history.
[*]The story files pass their schema and reference checks. The normal build is held for an update to its old nine-file inventory check; appearance, pacing, cards and older saves still await owner review in the game.
[/list]

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Written for the Phobos mods by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko), with AI-assisted drafting reviewed for the project. Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games or Kitfox Games.
Development notes record thematic influences from Ursula K. Le Guin, C. J. Cherryh and William Gibson. All writing is original; their characters, settings and prose are not adapted.
The cover is original Phobos promotional pixel art, generated with OpenAI Imagegen using other Phobos covers as style references. It shows spacers sharing a story between shifts; it is an illustration, not a gameplay screenshot.

